ate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.6553131765113094,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.027561984037534386,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":77.6,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.07403664784707363,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.006469116946290091,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":89.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.00607,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"American Healthcare REIT, Inc., a Maryland-based self-managed REIT, owns and operates a diversified portfolio of clinical healthcare real estate across the U.S., U.K., and the Isle of Man. Its focus includes senior housing, skilled nursing facilities (SNFs), outpatient medical (OM) buildings, and other healthcare-related properties. The company utilizes a fully integrated management platform and operates senior housing under the RIDEA structure. In addition to owning and operating properties, it has originated and acquired secured loans and may pursue other real estate-related investments opportunistically. The REIT seeks income-generating assets and selectively develops healthcare properties. It has elected to be taxed as a REIT under the U.S. Internal Revenue Code and intends to maintain compliance with REIT requirements. American Healthcare REIT, Inc. is based in Irvine, United States.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey T. Hanson | CEO & Chairman | Compensation: $200,563 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 121 people. Revenue per employee of $18.7M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 115%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $121K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["American Healthcare REIT, Inc. is a large-cap real estate business with a $13.4B market cap on $2.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +17% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 21% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 4.8\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 7.4% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 204% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Carries a 87% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8723839009287928},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Real Estate peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"American Healthcare REIT (AHR) Stock May Be 44% Undervalued After Raised Guidance","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-ahr/american-healthcare-reit/news/american-healthcare-reit-ahr-stock-may-be-44-undervalued-aft","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794575975.879,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.908,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Machina Capital S.A.S. Acquires New Shares in American Healthcare REIT, Inc. $AHR","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/machina-capital-s-a-s-acquires-new-shares-in-american-healthcare-reit-inc-ahr.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794566724.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.919,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"American Healthcare REIT (AHR) Upgraded to Strong Buy: Here's Why","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028905/american-healthcare-reit-ahr-upgraded-to-strong-buy-here-s-why?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_12_zacks_rank_upgrade-3028905","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794499202.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope